          },
          "message": "fix: fix issue, pull request, commit and status edge cases (#120)\n\n`gt issue create --blocked-by/--blocking` created the issue and then failed on a missing dependency; missing issues are now refused first. Pin, unpin and unlock acted again on items already in that state; like lock and gh, they now report it and change nothing, and issue and pull request JSON gains `locked` (and `pinned` for pull requests). Merging a pull request blocked by an open dependency surfaced a bare server error; it now names the blocking issues, and `gt pr view` tells a deleted head branch or open blockers apart from conflicts. `gt pr checks --required` named the head branch instead of the base branch. `gt commit pr` printed nothing without `--json` and failed on abbreviated SHAs. `gt status --json` printed `mentions: null`. `gt pr review --pending` named the wrong flag in its body error, `gt pr review reply` checked an empty body only after a request, and `gt time cancel` asked to discard a stopwatch that was not running.\n\nReviewed-on: https://gitea.com/gitea/cli/pulls/120\n",
          "tree": {
            "url": "https://gitea.com/api/v1/repos/gitea/cli/git/trees/a3258b91738509ba04083dffdd74180b09f0d278c882319fc55f77d1be6b9ba7",
