            "date": "2026-11-18T20:13:13Z"
          },
          "message": "fix: harden extensions, debug output, artifact names and Actions values (#119)\n\nLocal extensions ran whatever was at their recorded path. gt now follows links and refuses the target unless it is a regular file owned by the user or root that not every user can write to or replace. Group-writable files stay allowed for user-private groups. A missing one points to `gt extension remove`, and `gt extension list` marks it.\n\nThe commit an extension install resolves was printed and passed to git unchecked. It must now be a full commit ID.\n\n`--debug` printed transport errors, which can quote server text, unfiltered.\n\n`gt run download` used artifact names as directory names with weaker checks than `--zip`, and stopped on a bad name only after writing earlier artifacts. All names are now checked first.\n\n`secret set` and `variable set` silently changed values that were not UTF-8. They now refuse them.\n\nReviewed-on: https://gitea.com/gitea/cli/pulls/119\n",
          "tree": {
            "url": "https://gitea.com/api/v1/repos/gitea/cli/git/trees/788d564bbf317b27f1a05847c9a354130a761e7420e45878cefc8180876ece41",
